/*--- Choupo stream state.  Every DIMENSIONAL value carries its unit; the parser converts to SI.
     componentMolarFlows is the OVERALL material (all phases); a phases{} block, when present,
     is a decomposition that sums back to it exactly. ---*/

/*  DESIGN BASIS OF THIS FLOW (2026-10-05, DEV.md C35 item 11).

    This is the burner feed whose flue gas is FINISHING.dryer's drying
    medium, so its size is the DRYER's design, and it is sized by the
    dryer's own energy balance, not by trial:

      * declared target: the product leaves with NO free water
        (X_final = 0; Li2CO3 crystals carry free surface water only);
      * the dryer's energy floor (EvaporativeDryer.H, limit 3): with the
        solid leaving at its feed temperature T_w = 363.15 K the gas pays
        for F_gas cp_gas (T_gas - T_w) / lambda(T_w) of evaporation.  At the
        previous 39.08 kmol/h of fuel + air (flue gas at 950.58 K) the unit
        printed 338.6037 kg/h evaporated of 1792.4925 kg/h fed, i.e.
        8.6644 kg of water per kmol of gas -- LINEAR in F_gas while the
        CH4 : O2 : N2 ratio, hence the adiabatic flame temperature and the
        flue composition, is held;
      * minimum gas = 1792.4925 / 8.6644 = 206.88 kmol/h (5.294 x);
      * a 5 % margin on that minimum: 217.22 kmol/h, i.e. the previous
        feed scaled by 5.5585 with the SAME ratio.  The run then reports
        [complete-limited], X_final = 0, T_out = 385.3 K (22 K of approach
        above the wet solid), exhaust a_w = 0.22.

    WHY 5 % AND NOT A ROUNDER 20 %.  A 20 % margin was tried first and is
    NOT taken: at that gas rate the unit's own hand energy balance (a Watson
    latent heat, which goes to zero at water's critical temperature, 647 K,
    and the free water warmed as a liquid at a constant cp) admits a
    second, unphysical root above 647 K, and its bisection returned
    T_out = 672 K.  That is an engine finding (DEV.md C35 item 11), not
    something a case should hide by a choice of number -- but nor should a
    case be designed on a supercritical "evaporation".  At 5 % the run was
    measured to land on the physical root.

    So the burner exit temperature is unchanged and only the amount of hot
    gas grows.  Until 2026-10-05 this file carried 1/5.56 of this flow, and
    once the dryer stopped evaporating water no heat paid for (C26 slice 2)
    the product left at 98.5 wt% water.

    AFTER C35 ITEM 7 (2026-10-05, same day; no number here changed).  The
    basis above was computed on the dryer's floor as it then was, the
    solid's FEED temperature.  The floor is now the gas's WET-BULB
    temperature (346.30 K for this flue gas), so the same gas would pay for
    more water at its floor and the 5 % margin is wider than stated; the
    flow is kept, by ruling.  And the spurious root above 647 K that
    excluded a 20 % margin is fixed in the unit (the outlet is the first
    root above the floor, below water's Tc): the 20 % gas now returns
    T_out = 446.56 K, which `check_evaporative_dryer` arm (e) runs.  The
    floor change alone would have sent even THIS flow to that root (the
    first bisection midpoint on [346.30, 950.58] K is above Tc), so the two
    shipped together. */

componentMolarFlows
{
    CH4    5.5588 kmol/h;
    O2    44.4681 kmol/h;
    N2    167.1980 kmol/h;
}

T               298.15 K;
P               100000 Pa;
